# The build context is the repository root, shared by both images
# (server/Dockerfile and Dockerfile.web), so this can only exclude what
# *neither* needs. The front-end build wants nearly the whole checkout --
# src/app, public, scripts, and the config files at the root.
#
# The server image is kept small by its Dockerfile rather than by this file: it
# copies `server/`, `src/fs/`, and `src/history/` explicitly and nothing else,
# which is also what makes the import boundary visible there.

# Secrets, first. `Dockerfile.web` copies the checkout wholesale before
# building, so anything not excluded here lands in a layer of its build stage --
# and while the image that ships carries only `dist`, that intermediate one
# stays in the local build cache. `.env` holds the session secret and the
# database passwords.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
coverage
.git
.github
.claude
__screenshots__
.vitest-attachments

# Database dumps, which hold student files and password hashes.
dumps
